-- title:
--   Transport of a formal-group lift across 𝔪^N = 0
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, $k$ a field of characteristic $q$ and $E_0$ a Weierstrass curve over $k$ which is elliptic, whose formal group satisfies `IsDrinfeldBasisAdic ⊥ q 0 0`: for the zero ideal of $k$ there is a unit power series $u$ with $(E_0.\text{formalGroup}).\text{nthSeries } q = u \cdot \text{drinfeldDivisor } q\,0\,0$. Let $W_0$ be a complete discrete valuation domain, adically complete for its maximal ideal, with maximal ideal generated by $q$, together with a surjection $\mathrm{res}_0 : W_0 \to k$ whose kernel is that maximal ideal. Let $T$ be an artinian local $W_0$-algebra with a surjection $\mathrm{res}_T : T \to k$ whose kernel is $\mathfrak m_T$ and which is compatible with $\mathrm{res}_0$ along the structure map, let $G$ be a commutative formal group law over $T$ whose reduction along $\mathrm{res}_T$ is the formal group law of $E_0$, and let $N$ satisfy $\mathfrak m_T^{\,N} = 0$. Assume there exist a Weierstrass curve $E$ over $T$ with $E$ reduced along $\mathrm{res}_T$ equal to $E_0$, a formal group law $G_n$ over $T/\mathfrak m_T^{\,N}$ whose series is the Weierstrass formal group law of $E$ reduced mod $\mathfrak m_T^{\,N}$, and an isomorphism of formal group laws $\psi$ from $G_n$ to the reduction of $G$ mod $\mathfrak m_T^{\,N}$ (a power series with zero constant term, invertible linear coefficient, commuting with the two laws) all of whose coefficients agree with those of $X$ modulo the image of $\mathfrak m_T$. Then there exist a Weierstrass curve $E$ over $T$ reducing to $E_0$ along $\mathrm{res}_T$, a formal group law $G'$ over $T$ whose series is the Weierstrass formal group law of $E$, and an isomorphism of formal group laws $\psi$ from $G'$ to $G$ with $\mathrm{res}_T(\mathrm{coeff}_n\,\psi) = \delta_{n,1}$ for all $n$.
--
--   This is the final descent step in the Serre–Tate style existence argument: once the nilpotency index of $\mathfrak m_T$ has been exhausted, a lift of $E_0$ together with an identification of its formal group law with $G$ modulo $\mathfrak m_T^{\,N}$ is already such data over $T$ itself. It feeds the statement [`WeierstrassCurve.exists_map_eq_and_lawIso_of_isBaseChange_formalGroup_of_isArtinianRing_of_prime`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.exists_map_eq_and_lawIso_of_isBaseChange_formalGroup_of_isArtinianRing_of_prime), where the induction on small extensions is assembled.
